# Helvety Cloud constitution

Before any feature work, read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/architecture/ROADMAP.md`. Implement **one phase (P\*) at a time**.

## Must

- Zero knowledge: Helvety cannot decrypt vault content. No master key, escrow, or support content recovery.
- No account passwords. Supabase Auth: email OTP only. Vault unlock: WebAuthn PRF (session ≠ decrypt).
- Greenfield only in `helvety-cloud`. Never copy from `helvety` or `helvety-browser-extension-chromium`.
- Free-tier only in foundation: Supabase Free, Vercel Hobby. Omit Redis, Sentry, paid CI, analytics, etc.
- Vault I/O via `/api/v1` + Bearer JWT. Browser may use Supabase Auth SDK; must not use PostgREST for vault tables.
- Supabase project `qnoeiurmyyyuawkcifmw` (helvety-cloud, Zurich) only — never `bkdzeihxzvrkndjvyzye`.
- Prefer Supabase/Vercel MCP and schema-as-code (`docs/architecture/SCHEMA_WORKFLOW.md`).
- No misleading E2EE/recovery claims in UI or docs (`docs/architecture/LEGAL_REQUIREMENTS.md`).

## Must not

- Implement multiple roadmap phases in one go unless the user explicitly expands scope.
- Add paid SaaS “for best practice.”
- Public signup/billing without the live legal pack and acceptance gates (P-legal2). Counsel review is optional for risk, not a product gate.
